# W4-UI-2 V1: the construction menu's full interaction proof through the real window - every
# category tab, a locked cell (no command sent), an armed placement that actually builds, and a
# demolish of what was just built. Positions are data/ui/hud.txt's category_column_x (782) and
# construction.txt's own category y / grid_click_x / grid_click_y values, not guessed; the world
# tile (1156, 516) is the same one settlement_activity.script already proves free and buildable
# for type 501.
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
key b
wait frames 5

# Every one of the 8 category tabs switches (construction.txt's own y per category).
click_px 782 325
wait frames 2
expect title-lacks build
click_px 782 373
wait frames 2
click_px 782 418
wait frames 2
click_px 782 463
wait frames 2
click_px 782 508
wait frames 2
click_px 782 553
wait frames 2
click_px 782 598
wait frames 2
click_px 782 643
wait frames 2

# Back to "public" (y 325), a locked cell (public (1,0), id 580, construction.txt "state locked"):
# no command is sent - the title must never show it armed.
click_px 782 325
wait frames 2
click_px 885 330
wait frames 2
expect title-lacks build 580

# An unlocked cell (public (0,0), id 501): arm it, then place it on the proven-free tile.
click_px 833 330
wait frames 5
expect title build 501
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
checkpoint built

# Demolish mode: the placement panel is still open after the build (nothing in the world-click
# path closes it), so the pickaxe rectangle still resolves Cancel at first click (closing the
# panel, construction_placement_open_ -> false) - a second click at the same spot now resolves
# ToggleDemolish (DevInput's own demolish_ flag, independent of the armed type Cancel never
# clears). Then the just-built house itself.
click_px 996 736
wait frames 2
click_px 996 736
wait frames 5
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
checkpoint demolished

key esc
wait frames 5
quit
